I've been using Account Password Helper, a Chrome password manager worth a look.

[Free & open source] GPL-3.0, no account, no subscription, no ads — the code is public.
[Secure encryption] PBKDF2-SHA256 (600,000 rounds) derives the key; every field is encrypted with AES-256-GCM. Your master password and data stay on your device — nothing is uploaded to any server.
[Core features] One-click login fill (optional auto-login), built-in TOTP, exact-host isolation for dev / test / prod, a separately encrypted personal info vault, offline security check, and JSON / CSV import and export.

